---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy — OG Toolser"
  description="How OG Toolser handles data, cookies, files you upload, and advertising."
  canonicalPath="/privacy/"
>
  <div class="container static-page">
    <Breadcrumbs crumbs={[{ name: 'Home', path: '/' }, { name: 'Privacy', path: '/privacy/' }]} />
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p>
      All calculations on OG Toolser run locally in your browser. Numbers and text you enter into
      a calculator or converter are never sent to our servers — this site has no backend that
      receives or stores what you type.
    </p>

    <h2>Files you upload (Bank Statement Converter, image compression tools)</h2>
    <p>
      A small number of tools — the <a href="/finance/bank-statement-converter/">Bank Statement
      Converter</a> and the <a href="/image/">image compression tools</a> — work with files you
      choose from your device, rather than plain text. Those files are the same as any other
      input on this site: read and processed entirely in your browser (using PDF.js for statements
      and the Canvas API for images) and never transmitted to a server, because there is no server
      endpoint on this site that accepts file uploads. Closing or reloading the tab discards
      everything — nothing is retained after your session ends. The Bank Statement Converter
      additionally limits uploads to 20MB and only reads the text layer of a PDF; see that tool's
      own page for its full accuracy and limitations notes.
    </p>

    <h2>Analytics</h2>
    <p>
      This site uses Google Analytics (gtag.js) to understand which tools are used, in aggregate.
      Google Analytics uses cookies and may process standard web analytics data (such as
      approximate location derived from IP address, device/browser type, and pages visited) under
      Google's own privacy policy. It does not receive the content you type or upload into any
      calculator, converter, or the Bank Statement Converter — those never leave your browser in
      the first place, so there's nothing for analytics to capture. You can block or limit this
      via your browser's tracking protection, an ad blocker, or Google's own opt-out tools.
    </p>

    <h2>Advertising</h2>
    <p>
      OG Toolser is supported by display advertising. Ad partners may use cookies to serve relevant
      ads; you can control this through your browser or ad-network opt-out settings.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .static-page {
    max-width: var(--tool-width);
    padding: var(--space-8) 0 var(--space-10);
  }
</style>
